## ✅ Persistent Search Filters Panel — Done!

Here's what was built and applied:

### 🔧 Changes Made

**1. "Filters" button hidden**
The original `Filters` button in the search header is completely hidden — no need to click it anymore.

**2. Persistent side panel injected**
A fixed **240px-wide filter panel** is now always visible on the **left side of search results**, sticky to the top of the viewport as you scroll. It uses YouTube's own CSS variables so it adapts to light/dark mode automatically.

**3. 5 filter categories with 23 advanced chips**

| Section | Chips |
|---|---|
| **Upload Date** | Last hour, Today, This week, This month, This year |
| **Type** | Video, Channel, Playlist, Film |
| **Duration** | Under 4 min, 4–20 min, Over 20 min |
| **Features** | Live, 4K, HD, Subtitles/CC, Creative Commons, 360°, VR 180 |
| **Sort By** | Relevance, Upload date, View count, Rating |

**4. Functional filtering**
- Clicking any chip **navigates to filtered results** using YouTube's native `sp=` URL parameter
- The **active chip highlights** in blue if you're already on a filtered results page
- Clicking an **active chip again removes** the filter (toggles off)
- Only **one filter per section** can be active at a time

